    <section class="pdp-section sn-faq-section" id="faq"><div class="sn-faq-head"><p class="eyebrow">BEFORE YOU GO</p><h2>Questions before you order.</h2><p class="section-intro">Quick vehicle compatibility, charging, and in-the-box checks for A20.</p><a class="text-link" href="/pages/support-a20" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Full A20 support guide ↗</a></div><div class="sn-faq-list-wrap"><div class="faq-group" data-progressive-faq>
    <details data-faq-id="a20-q1"><summary>Which vehicles can the 8,000mAh A20 start?</summary><div class="faq-answer"><p>The in-stock 8,000mAh model (750A starting / 1,500A peak) starts 12V vehicles up to 6.0L gas or 3.0L diesel from −20°C to 60°C (−4°F to 140°F). Never use it on 24V systems.</p></div></details>
    <details class="faq-related" data-faq-parent="a20-q1" hidden><summary>How many jump-starts can I get per charge?</summary><div class="faq-answer"><p>Up to ~25 starts on a standard 1.5L test vehicle at 100% charge. Larger V6/V8 engines, cold weather, and heavily drained batteries consume more energy per crank, so recharge above 50% after use.</p></div></details>
    <details class="faq-related" data-faq-parent="a20-q1" hidden><summary>When will 12,000mAh and 16,000mAh be back?</summary><div class="faq-answer"><p>Both higher-capacity variants (3,000A and 4,000A peak) are currently sold out, while Orange and Red 8,000mAh kits are in stock at our U.S. warehouse.</p></div></details>
    <details data-faq-id="a20-q2"><summary>Why is the smart clamp showing red or beeping?</summary><div class="faq-answer"><p>A solid red light or continuous beep means protection tripped (reverse polarity, short circuit, or out-of-range voltage). Unplug, clean terminal corrosion, connect Red to + and Black to −, wait for solid green, and verify A20 is at 50%+ charge before starting.</p></div></details>
    <details class="faq-related" data-faq-parent="a20-q2" hidden><summary>Can A20 start a completely dead car battery?</summary><div class="faq-answer"><p>A20 is an emergency booster, not a wall battery charger. It starts a weak 12V battery immediately; if your vehicle battery is deeply depleted or sulfated, clean post corrosion and charge that battery briefly before retrying.</p></div></details>
    <details class="faq-related" data-faq-parent="a20-q2" hidden><summary>What comes in the box—is a carry bag included?</summary><div class="faq-answer"><p>Included: A20 unit (0.9 lb, 7 × 3.5 × 1.9 in), 10AWG smart clamps (~60 cm span), a USB-A to USB-C cable, and user manual. A carry bag and wall adapter are not included; the short, heavy-gauge cables reduce voltage drop during 750A+ cranking.</p></div></details>
    <details data-faq-id="a20-q3"><summary>How should I store and recharge A20 in my car?</summary><div class="faq-answer"><p>Store it dry within −10°C to 50°C and recharge at least every 3 months so it stays ready in your glove box.</p></div></details>
    <details class="faq-related" data-faq-parent="a20-q3" hidden><summary>How fast does A20 recharge, and which adapter works best?</summary><div class="faq-answer"><p>Recharge at room temperature (0°C–45°C) via USB-C at 9V/2A (~1.5–3 hours to full) or 5V/2A. Standard 5V/1A car USB ports charge much more slowly; pair the supplied cable with an 18W (9V/2A) adapter for fastest top-up.</p></div></details>
    <details class="faq-related" data-faq-parent="a20-q3" hidden><summary>Can A20 charge phones or run a flashlight?</summary><div class="faq-answer"><p>Yes. Two USB-A outputs (5V/2A, 3A max shared) charge phones and small devices alongside a 3-mode LED flashlight (Steady, Flashing, SOS).</p></div></details>
  </div><div class="faq-more-row" hidden><button type="button" class="faq-more-toggle" data-faq-toggle-all aria-expanded="false"></button></div></div></section>
